# SABOTAGE: ADR-052 §2.1 item 1 — the LiveView wide-event handler loses its rescue/catch. One
# malformed metadata map then raises inside the :telemetry callback, :telemetry DETACHES the
# handler, and the plane goes dark for the rest of the node's life with no error to the caller.
#
# Flips the total-callback test (the malformed-map test alone cannot see it: the builder is total
# over every map shape Phoenix sends, so the rescue is what covers the shapes it does not).
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/observability/live_telemetry_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: handle_event/4 returns :ok for ANY input
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/observability/live_telemetry.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/observability/live_telemetry.ex
index 8f24986..6055d9b 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/observability/live_telemetry.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/observability/live_telemetry.ex
@@ -105,11 +105,9 @@ defmodule Samen.Observability.LiveTelemetry do
       :skip -> :ok
     end
 
+    # SABOTAGE (ADR-052 §2.1): the handler no longer guards itself — a malformed metadata map
+    # raises out of the telemetry callback and :telemetry detaches it for good.
     :ok
-  rescue
-    _ -> :ok
-  catch
-    _, _ -> :ok
   end
 
   @doc false
